> Module Tax_rates

> Using Types
> Using Rounding as R

# Tax rate schedules and the Tax Table midpoint (Form 1040 line 16)

Direct File module `taxCalculations.xml`, facts `/roundedTaxableIncome`
(line 282) and `/tentativeTaxFromTaxableIncome` (line 424). Issue #10.

Form 1040 line 16 reads: "Tax (see instructions). Check if any from: ..."
(`sources/forms-instructions/f1040--2024.pdf` p 2). The 1040 instructions
say to find the tax in the Tax Table (taxable income under $100,000) or with
the Tax Computation Worksheet ($100,000 or more)
(`sources/forms-instructions/i1040gi--2024.pdf` pp 64 to 76).

Out of scope here (scope.md section 2.1, issue #10): the Qualified Dividends
and Capital Gain Tax Worksheet, Schedule D Tax Worksheet, kiddie tax (Forms
8814, 8615), Form 4972 and the Foreign Earned Income Tax Worksheet. Direct
File does not compute them either.

The rate schedules are declared in this module, not in `Params_2024`, so this
issue touches only its own files. They can move to `Params_2024` without a
change of meaning.

## 26 U.S.C. § 1(j)(2): the 2024 rate tables

Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.01, `sources/revproc/rp-23-34.pdf` pp 5 to 7:
"For taxable years beginning in 2024, the tax rate tables under § 1 are as
follows". Table 1 is § 1(j)(2)(A) "Married Individuals Filing Joint Returns
and Surviving Spouses" (p 5), Table 2 is § 1(j)(2)(B) "Heads of Households"
(pp 5 to 6), Table 3 is § 1(j)(2)(C) "Unmarried Individuals (other than
Surviving Spouses and Heads of Households)" (p 6), Table 4 is § 1(j)(2)(D)
"Married Individuals Filing Separate Returns" (pp 6 to 7). Each row reads
"Over $X but not over $Y: $B plus R% of the excess over $X".

Source typo, not copied: in Tables 2, 3 and 4 the printed 32% row says "the
excess over $191,150". The row header "Over $191,950" (same row) and the
printed Tax Table show the bound is $191,950 (`sources/VERIFICATION.md`).

Form: the marginal form of `sources/CATALA_PATTERNS.md` section 6. Each
bracket has a lower bound, an upper bound and a rate; the tax is the sum of
rate times the slice of income inside each bracket. The statutory cumulative
base (the "$B" of the table) is stored too, only so that a test can check
that the two forms agree and that the bases chain: base(n) = base(n-1) +
rate(n-1) * (upper(n-1) - lower(n-1)).

```catala-metadata
## One row of a rate table: income from `lower` up to `upper` is taxed at
## `rate`; `base` is the table's "$B plus ..." amount, i.e. the tax on
## `lower`. The top bracket has no statutory upper bound; its `upper` is the
## sentinel `no_upper_bound`.
declaration structure Bracket:
  data lower content money
  data upper content money
  data rate content decimal
  data base content money

## Sentinel upper bound of the top bracket ("Over $731,200" has no limit).
## One trillion dollars; no taxable income reaches it.
declaration no_upper_bound content money equals $1,000,000,000,000

# Rev. Proc. 2023-34 Table 1, § 1(j)(2)(A), rp-23-34.pdf p 5. Direct File
# /tentativeTaxFromTaxableIncome, MFJ and QSS branch (lines 438 to 656).
## Married filing jointly and qualifying surviving spouse (§ 1(a), § 2(a)).
declaration schedule_mfj_qss content list of Bracket equals [
  Bracket { -- lower: $0       -- upper: $23,200   -- rate: 10% -- base: $0 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $23,200  -- upper: $94,300   -- rate: 12% -- base: $2,320 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $94,300  -- upper: $201,050  -- rate: 22% -- base: $10,852 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $201,050 -- upper: $383,900  -- rate: 24% -- base: $34,337 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $383,900 -- upper: $487,450  -- rate: 32% -- base: $78,221 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $487,450 -- upper: $731,200  -- rate: 35% -- base: $111,357 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $731,200 -- upper: no_upper_bound -- rate: 37% -- base: $196,669.50 }
]

# Rev. Proc. 2023-34 Table 2, § 1(j)(2)(B), rp-23-34.pdf pp 5 to 6 (the 32%
# row prints "excess over $191,150", a typo for $191,950). Direct File lines
# 658 to 872.
## Head of household (§ 1(b), § 2(b)).
declaration schedule_head_of_household content list of Bracket equals [
  Bracket { -- lower: $0       -- upper: $16,550   -- rate: 10% -- base: $0 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $16,550  -- upper: $63,100   -- rate: 12% -- base: $1,655 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $63,100  -- upper: $100,500  -- rate: 22% -- base: $7,241 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $100,500 -- upper: $191,950  -- rate: 24% -- base: $15,469 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $191,950 -- upper: $243,700  -- rate: 32% -- base: $37,417 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $243,700 -- upper: $609,350  -- rate: 35% -- base: $53,977 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $609,350 -- upper: no_upper_bound -- rate: 37% -- base: $181,954.50 }
]

# Rev. Proc. 2023-34 Table 3, § 1(j)(2)(C), rp-23-34.pdf p 6 (same $191,150
# typo in the 32% row). Direct File lines 874 to 1088.
## Single: unmarried individuals who are not surviving spouses or heads of
## households (§ 1(c)).
declaration schedule_single content list of Bracket equals [
  Bracket { -- lower: $0       -- upper: $11,600   -- rate: 10% -- base: $0 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $11,600  -- upper: $47,150   -- rate: 12% -- base: $1,160 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $47,150  -- upper: $100,525  -- rate: 22% -- base: $5,426 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $100,525 -- upper: $191,950  -- rate: 24% -- base: $17,168.50 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $191,950 -- upper: $243,725  -- rate: 32% -- base: $39,110.50 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $243,725 -- upper: $609,350  -- rate: 35% -- base: $55,678.50 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $609,350 -- upper: no_upper_bound -- rate: 37% -- base: $183,647.25 }
]

# Rev. Proc. 2023-34 Table 4, § 1(j)(2)(D), rp-23-34.pdf pp 6 to 7 (same
# typo). Same as Single through $243,725; the 35% bracket ends at $365,600.
# Direct File lines 1090 to 1300.
## Married filing separately (§ 1(d)).
declaration schedule_married_separate content list of Bracket equals [
  Bracket { -- lower: $0       -- upper: $11,600   -- rate: 10% -- base: $0 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $11,600  -- upper: $47,150   -- rate: 12% -- base: $1,160 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $47,150  -- upper: $100,525  -- rate: 22% -- base: $5,426 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $100,525 -- upper: $191,950  -- rate: 24% -- base: $17,168.50 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $191,950 -- upper: $243,725  -- rate: 32% -- base: $39,110.50 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $243,725 -- upper: $365,600  -- rate: 35% -- base: $55,678.50 };
  Bracket { -- lower: $365,600 -- upper: no_upper_bound -- rate: 37% -- base: $98,334.75 }
]

## The rate table that applies to a filing status. Direct File selects the
## schedule with `/isFilingStatusMFJ or /isFilingStatusQSS`,
## `/isFilingStatusHOH`, `/isFilingStatusSingle` and `/isFilingStatusMFS`.
declaration schedule_for content list of Bracket
  depends on status content Types.FilingStatus
  equals
    match status with pattern
    -- MarriedFilingJointly: schedule_mfj_qss
    -- QualifyingSurvivingSpouse: schedule_mfj_qss
    -- HeadOfHousehold: schedule_head_of_household
    -- Single: schedule_single
    -- MarriedFilingSeparately: schedule_married_separate

## Tax on `income` by the marginal form: the sum, over the brackets of
## `table`, of the rate times the part of `income` inside the bracket. Not
## rounded to the dollar.
declaration marginal_tax content money
  depends on
    table content list of Bracket,
    income content money
  equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each b among table to
        (Money.positive of ((Money.min of income, b.upper) - b.lower)) * b.rate)

## Tax on `income` by the table's cumulative form: "$B plus R% of the excess
## over $X" for the row that contains `income` ("not over" bounds are
## inclusive). Not rounded to the dollar. For `income` at or below zero it is 0.
declaration cumulative_tax content money
  depends on
    table content list of Bracket,
    income content money
  equals
    if income <= $0 then $0 else
    Money.sum of
      (map each b among
        (list of b among table such that income > b.lower and income <= b.upper)
        to (b.base + (income - b.lower) * b.rate))
```

## 1040 line 16, step one: the Tax Table midpoint (`/roundedTaxableIncome`)

Direct File does not store the printed Tax Table. Its description of
`/roundedTaxableIncome` reads: "Income less than $100,000 uses the tax tables
from the Instructions for Form 1040. This fact selects the "midpoint" that
corresponds to each entry in the tax tables, for use in calculating tenative
tax." The Tax Table rows are 5 dollars wide up to $25 (three hard-coded
midpoints), then $25 rows to $3,000 and $50 rows to $100,000
(`i1040gi--2024.pdf` pp 64 to 65); from $100,000 the Tax Computation
Worksheet uses the exact income (p 76). The tax of a row is the schedule
applied to the row's midpoint and rounded.

The cases in the XML, in order, are: taxable income at most 0 gives 0; under
5 gives 2.50; under 15 gives 10; under 25 gives 20; under 3,000 gives
`StepwiseMultiply(TI, 25/25) + 12.50`; under 100,000 gives
`StepwiseMultiply(TI, 50/50) + 25`; otherwise TI itself.

```catala-metadata
## Direct File `/roundedTaxableIncome`: the value the rate schedule is applied
## to. `R.stepwise_multiply` drops the cents and rounds down to the bottom of
## the $25 or $50 row; the midpoint is then 12.50 or 25 above it.
declaration rounded_taxable_income_of content money
  depends on taxable_income content money
  equals
    if taxable_income <= $0 then $0
    else if taxable_income < $5 then $2.50
    else if taxable_income < $15 then $10
    else if taxable_income < $25 then $20
    else if taxable_income < $3,000 then
      R.stepwise_multiply of taxable_income, 25, 25 + $12.50
    else if taxable_income < $100,000 then
      R.stepwise_multiply of taxable_income, 50, 50 + $25
    else taxable_income
```

## 1040 line 16, step two: the rate schedule (`/tentativeTaxFromTaxableIncome`)

Direct File applies the schedule of the filing status to `/roundedTaxableIncome`
and rounds the result to the dollar (`Round` around the whole `Switch`).

```catala-metadata
## Line 16 as a function of taxable income and filing status: the marginal
## tax on the Tax Table midpoint, rounded to the dollar (half up).
declaration tentative_tax_for content money
  depends on
    taxable_income content money,
    filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (marginal_tax of
        (schedule_for of filing_status),
        (rounded_taxable_income_of of taxable_income))

## The same by the cumulative "$B plus R% of the excess" form.
declaration tentative_tax_cumulative_for content money
  depends on
    taxable_income content money,
    filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (cumulative_tax of
        (schedule_for of filing_status),
        (rounded_taxable_income_of of taxable_income))

## Form 1040 line 16 for the supported cases: no capital gain worksheet, no
## Schedule D, no kiddie tax.
declaration scope TentativeTax:
  ## Form 1040 line 15, taxable income (Direct File `/taxableIncome`).
  input taxable_income content money
  ## Direct File `/filingStatus`.
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  ## Direct File `/roundedTaxableIncome`.
  output rounded_taxable_income content money
  ## Direct File `/tentativeTaxFromTaxableIncome`: Form 1040 line 16.
  output tentative_tax_from_taxable_income content money
  ## Same value by the cumulative "$B plus R%" form of the rate tables; kept
  ## so tests can check the two forms agree.
  output tentative_tax_cumulative_form content money
```

```catala
scope TentativeTax:
  definition rounded_taxable_income equals
    rounded_taxable_income_of of taxable_income

  # Rounding: one `round` (half up) of the exact sum, as DF's `Round`.
  # Per-slice products are rounded to the cent by Catala, DF rounds once
  # after adding the base; the Tax Table test shows no difference (Q-R2).
  definition tentative_tax_from_taxable_income equals
    tentative_tax_for of taxable_income, filing_status

  definition tentative_tax_cumulative_form equals
    tentative_tax_cumulative_for of taxable_income, filing_status
```
